WEBVTT

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:50.380
The rear is sliding.

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:51.650
I know that...

00:01:51.650 --> 00:01:54.130
Your acceleration's also bad. Accelerate more!

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:56.340
You say it so easily...

00:01:56.340 --> 00:02:00.390
To accelerate more, I need to be rather skillful and courageous.

00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:03.600
Because we set it like this.

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:07.100
I guess Akio has his hands full...

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:18.630
This guy is too restless. I can't handle this all the way.

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:33.060
We've kept you waiting, Akio.

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:35.500
The settings for the carburetor turbo are complete.

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:46.610
<i>Now, this place...</i>

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:49.510
Steering Monthly
Tuning Monthly
NK Production

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:03.540
Is this too much?

00:03:04.460 --> 00:03:08.660
No, it's alright. You wrote much better compared to 2 years ago.

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:11.790
But there's one thing I'm worried about.

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:17.050
Frankly, I feel that there's something you're not telling to readers.

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:20.760
Perhaps, when you wrote this you thought
that it's alright if it wasn't published?

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:25.050
You knew? Of course you would.

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:26.760
Why?

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:35.690
At the beginning, I wanted to write
about Flat Racing's Takayuki Kuroki,

00:03:35.690 --> 00:03:39.610
how old-fashioned as a tuner he is.

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:45.850
While writing, I felt that this would not
be understood by the readers.

00:03:45.850 --> 00:03:52.120
But even so, that's alright. Honestly, I wrote this for myself.

00:03:54.090 --> 00:03:56.880
That's just like you.

00:03:56.880 --> 00:04:02.360
Even though it won't be published,
I'll still write about him until the end.

00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:05.640
Even if I were to be the last one.

00:04:08.110 --> 00:04:10.940
This time, I won't run away.

00:04:26.090 --> 00:04:27.660
You're here already, Mika.

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:31.610
You always leave it wide open. You're really careless.

00:04:32.770 --> 00:04:36.100
I have nothing that can be stolen.

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:37.300
Did you go for a drive?

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:39.380
Just a little around here.

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:42.380
See you then, Kuroki-san.

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:44.390
Yeah, later.

00:04:47.060 --> 00:04:49.890
It's rare to see a Porsche, is he a customer?

00:04:49.890 --> 00:04:54.210
No, he isn't. You should have heard about him too before.

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:55.640
BlackBird.

00:04:55.640 --> 00:04:58.150
BlackBird? That?

00:04:58.150 --> 00:05:03.610
Yes, Emperor of Wangan, the black seabird. He is BlackBird.

00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:05.800
Him?

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:07.190
Was it as you expected?

00:05:07.190 --> 00:05:09.150
Or was your image different?

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:12.860
He doesn't seem like your friend...

00:05:12.860 --> 00:05:15.880
That's wrong, I'm still far from him.

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:21.900
But in some respects, he is frighteningly close to me.

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:25.480
You mean, like the fact he has the instinct to keep on racing?

00:05:25.480 --> 00:05:27.640
You seem to be very happy, Taka.

00:05:28.910 --> 00:05:31.900
Guess I can't deceive you. True to say, I'm happy.

00:05:31.900 --> 00:05:36.050
Because it seems like I was accepted
by him and the people around him.

00:05:38.490 --> 00:05:41.150
You all get together as if you were magnets.

00:05:41.670 --> 00:05:45.540
Somebody with the same level of speed whom you can discuss with.

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:49.710
Are you going out?

00:05:49.710 --> 00:05:51.670
Yes, for a while.

00:05:51.670 --> 00:05:52.860
I'll go too-

00:05:52.860 --> 00:05:53.660
No.

00:05:53.660 --> 00:05:57.260
I'm going alone. I just need to drive for a while.

00:05:57.260 --> 00:06:02.550
My body is too hot, so I just need to cool
down or the problem won't be solved.

00:06:04.600 --> 00:06:05.310
Later.

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:32.910
<i>A car is a machine. It is just a tool to let you run faster.</i>

00:06:33.550 --> 00:06:38.410
<i>It's good enough if it meets the requirements
of the driver accurately and specifically.</i>

00:06:39.060 --> 00:06:41.620
<i>It's something that is neither more nor less than that.</i>

00:06:54.610 --> 00:06:56.390
<i>But this guy is different.</i>

00:06:57.200 --> 00:07:00.390
<i>In that Z, there's something in it which it not like a normal machine.</i>

00:07:00.790 --> 00:07:02.040
<i>I have to admit that.</i>

00:07:18.770 --> 00:07:21.000
<i>Tominaga, Kitami.</i>

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:23.910
<i>The carburetor turbo which was set by them,</i>

00:07:24.640 --> 00:07:27.440
<i>he's giving it his all to overcome it.</i>

00:07:27.440 --> 00:07:31.070
<i>If I let my guard down for even a split
second, it seems he will pull away</i>

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:46.350
<i>It's true we completed its setting, but please don't misunderstand.</i>

00:07:46.350 --> 00:07:49.520
<i>All we can do is what we have done.</i>

00:07:52.210 --> 00:07:56.860
<i>Setting has no end, once it starts to run, there'll surely be problems.</i>

00:07:56.860 --> 00:07:59.580
<i>After fixing the problems, you run again.</i>

00:08:01.910 --> 00:08:04.330
<i>And repeat it again and again.</i>

00:08:04.330 --> 00:08:08.130
<i>We finish a car, as if raising something that's alive.</i>

00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:15.140
<i>Akio, after this point, it's all up to you.</i>

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:32.150
Sorry to made you wait.

00:08:32.150 --> 00:08:34.500
Sorry for calling you out.

00:08:34.500 --> 00:08:38.310
I don't mind. Anyway, work was just over
so I was thinking about going out, too.

00:08:38.310 --> 00:08:40.360
As expected Reina-chan, you understand me too.

00:08:41.900 --> 00:08:44.970
We're connected to each other just like magnets.

00:08:57.420 --> 00:09:01.430
<i>I feel like the heat from the engine is
passing to me through the steering.</i>

00:09:01.430 --> 00:09:05.940
<i>This is bad, why are both you and me so hot?</i>

00:09:06.910 --> 00:09:10.940
<i>You know it too? Yes, we will definitely meet.</i>

00:09:11.490 --> 00:09:13.440
<i>Tonight, with that Z.</i>

00:09:14.910 --> 00:09:17.710
Normally he wouldn't say something like that,

00:09:17.710 --> 00:09:20.950
so I felt they're powerfully calling out to each other tonight.

00:09:20.950 --> 00:09:26.460
Taka and the guy in the Z, and also Reina-chan and BlackBird.

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:32.170
Taka said that if you wished for it too, you can meet Z.

00:09:32.170 --> 00:09:36.480
It all depends on our desires.

00:09:39.690 --> 00:09:42.680
<i>I just wanted to check out the situation for a while, but...</i>

00:09:55.390 --> 00:09:59.450
Is it all right, suddenly turning off the engine without after-idling?

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:03.450
I'm afraid not. I just want to check the burning of the plug.

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:06.390
When it's idle it's wet, right?

00:10:12.590 --> 00:10:14.300
They look wet.

00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:18.460
Yeah, that means I'm not accelerating enough.

00:10:21.400 --> 00:10:24.970
You understood? You're sharp as expected.

00:10:25.460 --> 00:10:29.350
<i>These six are synchronized and were burnt similarly.</i>

00:10:30.180 --> 00:10:34.190
For this Z, the sixth normally tends to burnout,

00:10:34.790 --> 00:10:39.080
even though I have changed the settings in various ways.

00:10:39.080 --> 00:10:41.700
But all six of them never burned in the same way before.

00:10:46.800 --> 00:10:50.900
Kitami-san and Tominaga-san are really amazing people,

00:10:50.900 --> 00:10:54.820
it's as if they can communicate with the engine.

00:10:54.820 --> 00:10:57.710
But they can't drive the car skillfully.

00:10:57.710 --> 00:11:01.670
That's right, this setting is probably at the very limit.

00:11:01.670 --> 00:11:05.440
If I'm careless even a little, this guy will try to throw me out.

00:11:05.440 --> 00:11:07.220
It's a terribly restless thing.

00:11:08.150 --> 00:11:11.360
Anyway, Tominaga-san has reset the settings for you too, right?

00:11:11.360 --> 00:11:14.150
Compared to last time, it doesn't seem to be accelerating much.

00:11:14.150 --> 00:11:16.450
It didn't look like its usual self.

00:11:18.200 --> 00:11:22.240
It's a little late, but now I understand one more thing about this guy.

00:11:22.900 --> 00:11:28.010
The various settings which I made myself, was sort of like crippling it.

00:11:30.310 --> 00:11:34.960
In order to let it last a little longer, to save more energy,

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:39.650
I consciously avoid some dangerous and radical settings.

00:11:39.650 --> 00:11:42.460
But, that's not Z's true character.

00:11:42.950 --> 00:11:47.270
In this time now, and only in that time, running at maximum.

00:11:47.270 --> 00:11:48.970
That is what defines Z.

00:11:51.110 --> 00:11:52.290
What are you going to do tonight?

00:11:53.220 --> 00:11:56.740
I'm going up Yokonane Line and onto C1.

00:11:58.040 --> 00:11:58.830
I got it.

00:12:06.740 --> 00:12:11.910
<i>How skillfully does he drive that dangerous machine.</i>

00:12:12.600 --> 00:12:14.950
<i>How can you trust it so much?</i>

00:12:14.950 --> 00:12:17.750
<i>Why do you hold on to your feelings to that extent?</i>

00:12:20.260 --> 00:12:21.690
<i>I'm not good enough.</i>

00:12:22.460 --> 00:12:29.510
<i>After racing with Flat Racing's R33,
somewhere the flow has changed.</i>

00:12:29.510 --> 00:12:33.670
<i>I can't settle down. The reason is simple.</i>

00:12:33.670 --> 00:12:37.860
<i>At corners or straight roads, I couldn't be aggressive.</i>

00:12:37.860 --> 00:12:39.490
<i>Just a little, I was reducing acceleration.</i>

00:12:39.490 --> 00:12:42.020
<i>It was not functioning at its fullest.</i>

00:12:43.090 --> 00:12:46.170
<i>Can I not trust this machine anymore?</i>

00:12:47.040 --> 00:12:51.230
<i>He's pulling away, I cannot reach him.</i>

00:12:52.550 --> 00:13:00.770
<i>My motivation towards racing is crumbling now, ever so quickly.</i>

00:13:10.410 --> 00:13:14.870
The first time I went to gather materials
was right after graduating from university,

00:13:14.870 --> 00:13:18.430
at the tuner showdown, Yatabe High Speed Trial.

00:13:18.430 --> 00:13:20.060
You met Kuroki-san there?

00:13:20.060 --> 00:13:21.460
No.

00:13:21.460 --> 00:13:25.060
Actually, we met long time ago once.

00:13:26.420 --> 00:13:27.790
Where and when?

00:13:27.790 --> 00:13:31.300
It was 3 years earlier at Roppongi,

00:13:31.300 --> 00:13:35.040
when he was in his third year and I
was in my second year of university.

00:13:36.590 --> 00:13:39.590
At the joint party where I went just to fill up the empty spaces,

00:13:39.590 --> 00:13:43.190
Taka also seemed to have been called out for the same reason,

00:13:43.190 --> 00:13:45.090
the two of us were completely left out.

00:13:45.900 --> 00:13:50.340
Because we drove, we didn't drink and didn't talk much.

00:13:50.880 --> 00:13:56.010
I told him about this later but seems like he doesn't remember at all.

00:13:56.890 --> 00:13:58.760
Even though he was just sitting right next to me.

00:14:01.840 --> 00:14:05.710
After the first party, Taka was going home.

00:14:05.710 --> 00:14:10.200
I brought out my courage and asked him "could you send me home?".

00:14:10.710 --> 00:14:13.990
<i>I am sorry but my car is not suitable.</i>

00:14:14.960 --> 00:14:17.150
Taka's eyes made him seem like he was in a hurry.

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:22.500
I couldn't understand what he meant and was shocked.

00:14:23.160 --> 00:14:27.510
But now I understand, why his car is not suitable.

00:14:28.050 --> 00:14:31.620
I think he probably went off to Wangan alone after that.

00:14:31.620 --> 00:14:33.260
I guess so too.

00:14:33.800 --> 00:14:38.370
At that time, his heart had already been stolen by car tuning.

00:14:43.280 --> 00:14:45.770
<i>Where? Where is he?</i>

00:14:45.770 --> 00:14:49.270
In the two years when I was away from him,

00:14:50.350 --> 00:14:55.340
my job was exciting but, I felt as if I
was looking at something different.

00:14:56.990 --> 00:15:01.500
I understand. I also feel the same way.

00:15:08.220 --> 00:15:14.100
<i>"To go or to stop..."
Normal people will never understand its meaning.</i>

00:15:14.100 --> 00:15:17.260
<i>but in the end, for us, we only have these two choices.</i>

00:15:17.260 --> 00:15:20.810
<i>If you already decided to go, just go for it.</i>

00:15:20.810 --> 00:15:23.960
<i>"I don't want to lose it."
"I want to continue protecting it."</i>

00:15:23.960 --> 00:15:27.030
<i>"I just want to stay as it is now for a while longer."</i>

00:15:27.630 --> 00:15:31.020
<i>Somewhere inside, you, and us too, were secretly wishing for that.</i>

00:15:31.020 --> 00:15:34.100
<i>But those kinds of things don't define the Z anymore.</i>

00:15:34.100 --> 00:15:39.040
<i>Above all else, we are doing what Z itself does not want.</i>

00:15:39.040 --> 00:15:42.540
<i>I know it all too well, and even though I know it...</i>

00:15:43.010 --> 00:15:49.180
<i>Just knowing that in my head, I'm afraid of
seeing Z hurt someone right before my eyes.</i>

00:15:49.180 --> 00:15:52.300
<i>I unconsciously look away to protect myself.</i>

00:15:52.300 --> 00:15:55.550
<i>There's only one person who's looking straight.</i>

00:15:55.550 --> 00:15:57.550
<i>It was solely Reina.</i>

00:15:57.550 --> 00:16:00.050
<i>Z wants to run too, Akio.</i>

00:16:00.910 --> 00:16:03.800
<i>No other car has this desire for speed.</i>

00:16:03.800 --> 00:16:08.060
<i>To develop its potential until the limit is our duty.</i>

00:16:08.060 --> 00:16:13.580
<i>And the only person who can drive it, who was chosen by Z, is you.</i>

00:16:19.390 --> 00:16:20.260
We meet.

00:16:20.260 --> 00:16:21.330
As we expected.

00:16:32.840 --> 00:16:37.590
<i>The boost doesn't start properly.
The intake temperature is also too high.</i>

00:16:37.590 --> 00:16:39.450
<i>The oil pressure is lower than what I expected.</i>

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:45.850
<i>The more I run, the more I have to tun again. It's still far from perfect.</i>

00:16:45.850 --> 00:16:49.070
<i>But tonight we can meet. Definitely.</i>

00:16:55.950 --> 00:16:57.410
Next is Taka.

00:16:57.410 --> 00:16:59.650
Are you sure we meet so coincidently?

00:16:59.650 --> 00:17:02.660
I'm sure, it's because tonight's special.

00:17:03.020 --> 00:17:06.160
We met because we call out to each other.

00:17:06.160 --> 00:17:09.940
For him also, this place is his place now.

00:17:14.170 --> 00:17:17.350
<i>If I stop, then this is no longer Z.</i>

00:17:18.170 --> 00:17:22.190
<i>Even if, the engine were to give in tonight...</i>

00:17:25.190 --> 00:17:27.390
<i>I can surely meet you. You're near.</i>

00:18:09.690 --> 00:18:11.940
There's no need to force yourself to follow them, Reina-chan.

00:18:14.360 --> 00:18:18.300
<i>All the blood in my body is boiling, heated up.</i>

00:18:18.300 --> 00:18:21.450
<i>I'm a person who can be heated up to this level...</i>

00:18:30.600 --> 00:18:33.060
<i>I came to be fully convinced by that,</i>

00:18:33.060 --> 00:18:38.260
<i>I have been desiring such a life and death situation.</i>

00:18:38.260 --> 00:18:41.050
<i>So have you.</i>

00:18:48.230 --> 00:18:51.220
<i>Boost max .No unstable boosts.</i>

00:18:51.220 --> 00:18:54.730
<i>Oil pressure stable, no leaks. Oil temperature ok.</i>

00:18:54.730 --> 00:18:56.830
<i>Water temperature, exhaust temperature ok.</i>

00:18:56.830 --> 00:19:01.110
<i>AF value is the best. Acceleration is climbing.</i>

00:19:01.110 --> 00:19:03.510
<i>I can catch Z within my range completely!</i>

00:19:12.600 --> 00:19:15.210
No good, my timing was off.

00:19:15.210 --> 00:19:17.390
Dashing off suddenly after entering Wangan.

00:19:17.390 --> 00:19:19.260
We can't catch up with them any more like this.

00:19:19.260 --> 00:19:24.420
It's alright. Let's go to Hamazaki junction
from Rainbow Bridge and wait for them there.

00:19:31.440 --> 00:19:33.350
<i>I lost speed.</i>

00:19:33.350 --> 00:19:38.690
<i>Acceleration wasn't interrupted, but for an instant my leg tripped.</i>

00:19:39.790 --> 00:19:42.700
It's been a long time since I watched as a third party.

00:19:43.490 --> 00:19:46.740
This run brings about a rush of adrenaline.

00:19:46.740 --> 00:19:49.510
This can only be understood by the people who are present.

00:19:51.290 --> 00:19:57.390
In the end, even now, it's whether you can or
cannot accept what you see in front of you.

00:20:00.230 --> 00:20:03.000
Entering the world from the part time job during my university days,

00:20:03.000 --> 00:20:05.840
putting on an air of a great reporter,

00:20:05.840 --> 00:20:09.550
I wrote about the tuner's world considerably.

00:20:10.160 --> 00:20:13.550
The tuners improved their skills by accumulating experience.

00:20:13.550 --> 00:20:16.320
But in terms of financial and human relationship,

00:20:16.320 --> 00:20:19.610
they still remained as bad as they
were before and it got me frustrated.

00:20:19.610 --> 00:20:26.610
I was only watching Taka, thinking that this was for us.

00:20:26.610 --> 00:20:29.410
I wanted to change the rules of this world.

00:20:30.110 --> 00:20:32.850
At the very least, just for Flat Racing.

00:20:33.830 --> 00:20:37.840
But that was a very ignorant misunderstanding.

00:20:37.840 --> 00:20:42.340
What Taka told me at that time, I can now understand perfectly.

00:20:43.110 --> 00:20:46.390
<i>You can't hear the voice of the engine, can you?</i>

00:20:46.390 --> 00:20:47.820
<i>Voice?</i>

00:20:47.820 --> 00:20:50.390
<i>Yes, not the sound, but the voice.</i>

00:20:51.890 --> 00:20:55.870
<i>These machines called cars, run around this world.</i>

00:20:55.870 --> 00:21:00.850
<i>What we manufacture is a car, a living thing.</i>

00:21:01.420 --> 00:21:05.500
Not the past or something that will happen in the future,

00:21:05.500 --> 00:21:09.360
I want to watch the present Taka properly, and accept him too.

00:21:09.950 --> 00:21:14.370
I couldn't do it that time, because
I kept trying to look into the future.

00:21:14.370 --> 00:21:16.600
I couldn't see our future clearly.

00:21:20.900 --> 00:21:24.400
In the end, I thought the only way was to be separated.

00:21:25.800 --> 00:21:28.890
But it didn't solve anything.

00:21:29.600 --> 00:21:32.390
It's not a feeling that is deceived so easily.

00:21:32.390 --> 00:21:34.100
Mika-san...

00:21:34.100 --> 00:21:37.150
I recognize him, not for his past or for his future,

00:21:37.150 --> 00:21:40.340
but for who he is right in front of me now.

00:21:40.340 --> 00:21:43.150
That's my only answer.

00:21:52.360 --> 00:21:56.970
The two years I was away from Taka,
I distanced myself from this world,

00:21:56.970 --> 00:21:59.630
and I realized something else.

00:21:59.630 --> 00:22:01.420
Depending on the thing you are separated from,

00:22:01.420 --> 00:22:03.890
there will be something else which you'll find.

00:22:03.890 --> 00:22:07.390
Now, I can see what I couldn't see before.

00:22:08.820 --> 00:22:10.960
And so I couldn't help myself,

00:22:10.960 --> 00:22:15.890
and once more, I wanted to see the same
thing and be at the same place as Taka.

00:22:15.890 --> 00:22:22.060
With that in mind, I came back to see him again.

00:22:22.900 --> 00:22:27.600
<i>We are in sync, and can feel each other's acceleration clearly.</i>

00:22:27.600 --> 00:22:31.100
<i>At this speed, both our positions will be determined.</i>

00:22:33.610 --> 00:22:37.340
<i>We're repeating this rally with he greatest rhythm.</i>

00:22:43.310 --> 00:22:46.090
<i>The sense of speed loss that appeared
once, disappeared immediately.</i>

00:22:46.610 --> 00:22:48.640
<i>But will come back on more time.</i>

00:22:48.640 --> 00:22:52.640
<i>It's not the engine. Nor the fuel. Electricity?</i>

00:22:52.640 --> 00:22:55.660
<i>It's the misfiring! It will surely appear.</i>

00:22:55.660 --> 00:22:57.820
<i>After a minute? After a week?</i>

00:22:58.640 --> 00:23:02.350
<i>If misfiring happens at this speed,
the engine will blow in the worst case scenario.</i>

00:23:02.350 --> 00:23:04.850
<i>It won't be strange if anything happens right now.</i>

00:23:04.850 --> 00:23:07.860
<i>But you're also in the same boat as me,</i>

00:23:07.860 --> 00:23:10.420
<i>as long as you keep running at this place.</i>
